<title>NORWAY: Norway tax body rules in favour of Fokus.</title>
<headline>Norway tax body rules in favour of Fokus.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's fourth largest bank Fokus Bank said on Friday its tax-loss carried forward for 1996 had been increased to 2.2 billion crowns following a decision by the by superior tax commission.</p>
<p>The bank said the commission had given the bank its support that preference capital was to be treated as equity.</p>
<p>Fokus, along with Den norske Bank and Christiania Bank og Kreditkasse  all harbour tax carry-forwards from their deficit years in the early 1990s, when they plunged into a debt crisis over bad loans.</p>
<p>---Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
